      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The Curtain shader moves the vertices in the vertex stage, every frame. It changes where the curtain is drawn, not the mesh data stored in the project.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> This curtain has a Mesh Collider made from its mesh. In Play mode the ball rolls into it. Does it hit the cloth where you see it?\n\n<b>Try:</b> Press Play and watch the ball. Then select the curtain in the Scene view: compare the green outline of its Mesh Collider with the cloth.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Shader library, 3 \xB7 Curtain</color></size>"
